    <item>
    <title>Windows Configuration, Monitoring, and Troubleshooting</title>
    <link>https://example.com/post/windows-troubleshooting/</link>
    <pubDate>Fri, 09 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <author>Hafis Muhammad</author>
    <guid>https://example.com/post/windows-troubleshooting/</guid>
    <description>
        &lt;h5 id=&#34;system-configuration&#34;&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#system-configuration&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;
        &lt;svg class=&#34;icon&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; width=&#34;16&#34;&gt;
            &lt;path fill-rule=&#34;evenodd&#34;
                d=&#34;M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z&#34;&gt;
            &lt;/path&gt;
        &lt;/svg&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;
    System Configuration
&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;p&gt;System Configuration will help you to resolving issues, monitoring performance, making a configuration, checking the running servics, etc. You can launch the tools to make sure what you will do with this feature.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can use this shortut to open the tools by type Windows + Run and enter specific command like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Services -&amp;gt; services.msc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Registry -&amp;gt; regedit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programs -&amp;gt; appwizz.cpl&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network Connectiomn -&amp;gt; ncpa.cpl&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Command Prompt -&amp;gt; cmd&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct X Troubleshooter -&amp;gt; dxdiag&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Windows Version -&amp;gt; winver&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User Account -&amp;gt; netplwiz&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; 
    src=&#34;https://example.com/post/windows-troubleshooting/launch-tools.jpeg&#34; 
    alt=&#34;launch-tools&#34; 
     
    width=571 
    height=&#34;385&#34;  /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5 id=&#34;task-manager&#34;&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#task-manager&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;
        &lt;svg class=&#34;icon&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; width=&#34;16&#34;&gt;
            &lt;path fill-rule=&#34;evenodd&#34;
                d=&#34;M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z&#34;&gt;
            &lt;/path&gt;
        &lt;/svg&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;
    Task Manager
&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can monitor your application by resource usage here and background processes that running in your windows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; 
    src=&#34;https://example.com/post/windows-troubleshooting/task-manager.jpeg&#34; 
    alt=&#34;task manager&#34; 
     
    width=766 
    height=&#34;583&#34;  /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5 id=&#34;services&#34;&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#services&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;
        &lt;svg class=&#34;icon&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; width=&#34;16&#34;&gt;
            &lt;path fill-rule=&#34;evenodd&#34;
                d=&#34;M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z&#34;&gt;
            &lt;/path&gt;
        &lt;/svg&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;
    Services
&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can check the services running or the services that you don&amp;rsquo;t expected to be running here. I have had use this so much when I faced printing issue by restart the &lt;em&gt;print spooler&lt;/em&gt; service back then.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; 
    src=&#34;https://example.com/post/windows-troubleshooting/services-msc.jpeg&#34; 
    alt=&#34;services&#34; 
     
    width=806 
    height=&#34;593&#34;  /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5 id=&#34;registry&#34;&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#registry&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;
        &lt;svg class=&#34;icon&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; width=&#34;16&#34;&gt;
            &lt;path fill-rule=&#34;evenodd&#34;
                d=&#34;M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z&#34;&gt;
            &lt;/path&gt;
        &lt;/svg&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;
    Registry
&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I have also had a much issue with the passbook printer not working because sometimes the default printer names has changed, removed, and even I installed a new one but the printer still not response because the old name still there on the registry. So, I removed the printer name in the &lt;em&gt;registry&lt;/em&gt; then reinstalled it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; 
    src=&#34;https://example.com/post/windows-troubleshooting/regedit.jpeg&#34; 
    alt=&#34;registry&#34; 
     
    width=754 
    height=&#34;512&#34;  /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

    </description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
    <title>How to Install Windows Server 2025 in VMWare Fusion</title>
    <link>https://example.com/post/install-windows-server/</link>
    <pubDate>Fri, 22 Aug 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <author>Hafis Muhammad</author>
    <guid>https://example.com/post/install-windows-server/</guid>
    <description>
        &lt;p&gt;When I tried to use Windows Server 2025 in VMware Fusion on my Mac, I couldn’t find the ISO file on the Microsoft website. The ISO file must be in ARM architecture so that it can be run on VMware Fusion on a Mac. After watching many videos on YouTube, I found this website, &lt;a href=&#34;https://uupdump.net/&#34;&gt;https://uupdump.net/&lt;/a&gt;, which helped me to get the ISO file.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; 
    src=&#34;https://example.com/post/install-windows-server/win-server-2025.webp&#34; 
    alt=&#34;Windows Server 2025&#34; 
     
    width=640 
    height=&#34;360&#34;  /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&#34;download-windows-server-2025&#34;&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#download-windows-server-2025&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;
        &lt;svg class=&#34;icon&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; width=&#34;16&#34;&gt;
            &lt;path fill-rule=&#34;evenodd&#34;
                d=&#34;M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z&#34;&gt;
            &lt;/path&gt;
        &lt;/svg&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;
    Download Windows Server 2025
&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go to &lt;a href=&#34;https://uupdump.net/&#34;&gt;https://uupdump.net/&lt;/a&gt; and type ‘Windows Server Preview’ into the ‘Browse’ field
&lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; 
    src=&#34;https://example.com/post/install-windows-server/uup1.webp&#34; 
    alt=&#34;uup1&#34; 
     
    width=1400 
    height=&#34;851&#34;  /&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select the language you want to use, then Next
&lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; 
    src=&#34;https://example.com/post/install-windows-server/uup2.webp&#34; 
    alt=&#34;uup2&#34; 
     
    width=1400 
    height=&#34;851&#34;  /&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select edition, then Next
&lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; 
    src=&#34;https://example.com/post/install-windows-server/uup3.webp&#34; 
    alt=&#34;uup3&#34; 
     
    width=1400 
    height=&#34;851&#34;  /&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create download package
&lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; 
    src=&#34;https://example.com/post/install-windows-server/uup4.webp&#34; 
    alt=&#34;uup4&#34; 
     
    width=1400 
    height=&#34;851&#34;  /&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Once you have downloaded the package, you will receive a ZIP file, but this is not yet complete. To complete the download, you will need to use Terminal and follow the instructions under the ‘Create download package’ button until you get the ISO file.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; 
    src=&#34;https://example.com/post/install-windows-server/steps.webp&#34; 
    alt=&#34;steps&#34; 
     
    width=1400 
    height=&#34;332&#34;  /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&#34;install-windows-server-2025&#34;&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#install-windows-server-2025&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;
        &lt;svg class=&#34;icon&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; focusable=&#34;false&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; width=&#34;16&#34;&gt;
            &lt;path fill-rule=&#34;evenodd&#34;
                d=&#34;M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z&#34;&gt;
            &lt;/path&gt;
        &lt;/svg&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;
    Install Windows Server 2025
&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create a New Virtual Machine in VMware Fusion then add the ISO file. Follow these steps for installation:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; 
    src=&#34;https://example.com/post/install-windows-server/step1.webp&#34; 
    alt=&#34;step1&#34; 
     
    width=1400 
    height=&#34;1131&#34;  /&gt;
&lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; 
    src=&#34;https://example.com/post/install-windows-server/step2.webp&#34; 
